# English lives at the root, Chinese under /zh. /en was never a real tree —
# it 404s — but links in that shape may be out there, so they land on the
# English page they were meant for rather than on the 404.
/en           /          301!
/en/*         /:splat    301!

# No SPA fallback: the build prerenders a real HTML file for every route, so
# /pricing is dist/pricing/index.html rather than the shell with the router
# deciding afterwards. Anything unmatched falls through to 404.html, which
# the build also writes — a genuine 404 status instead of a 200 that renders
# a "page not found" body.
